{
  "about": "The value key of every scope kind. `cell` names a calendar cell by a date inside it (or a band, or two datetimes); `key` is the scope's key as it travels on the wire, and `text` its one canonical serialisation — what a column stores and what equality compares. The Rust ScopeKey and the TypeScript scope-key module must both produce exactly `text` from `cell`, and read `text` back to `key`. `window` is the scope's half-open `[start, end)` window in local wall-clock time — the Rust `ScopeKey::bounds` — which the TypeScript filter derives on its own, so both sides are held to it as well. See docs/adr/0009-derived-scopes.md.",
